---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'How is this different from the Merge PDF page?',
    a: 'Same engine, batch-first bench. This page is set up for the folder job: pick a whole folder of PDFs at once, sort the tray by file name in one click, and check every file\'s page count before you merge. The Merge PDF page is the same merge with hand ordering as the main act.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How many files can I merge?',
    a: 'As many as your device can hold in memory at once. On our bench, 25 one-page files merged in 71 milliseconds and the result was about 30% smaller than the biggest PDF site produced from the same 25 files. There is no counter here and no per-day allowance.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does merging change what is on the pages?',
    a: 'No. Pages are copied as they are, not re-drawn or recompressed. Text stays text, and the file sizes add up to roughly the sum of the parts.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where do my PDFs go?',
    a: 'Nowhere. They are read into this page and merged in your browser. Watch the network panel while it works if you want to check.',
  },
];
const faqJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
});
const howToJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HowTo',
  name: "How to merge a folder of PDFs at once",
  step: [
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 1, name: "Pick the folder or the files", text: "Drop PDFs on the tray, click to pick files, or use 'Pick a whole folder' to take every PDF in a folder at once. They are read into this page; they are never uploaded." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 2, name: "Put the files in order", text: "Sort the tray by file name in one click, or use the Up and Down buttons. The merged file follows the list, top to bottom." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 3, name: "Merge into one PDF", text: "Press 'Merge the batch into one PDF'. The page opens each PDF, copies its pages into a new file in list order, and saves." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 4, name: "Download the merged PDF", text: "Take the finished file away. Pages are copied, not rebuilt, so nothing is recompressed and nothing is lost." },
  ],
});
---

<Base title="Batch merge PDF: merge a folder of PDFs at once, free · Benchzy" description="Merge a whole folder of PDFs into one file in your order, inside your browser. Folder pick, name sort, page counts up front. No upload, no account, no file-count cap.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4">
    <section class="mt-8">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-deep">Job ticket · PDF bench · batch</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-black mt-2">Batch merge PDF</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        The folder is the job: a month of invoices, a scanner's worth of pages, a whole class of
        forms. Pick the folder, check the order, take one file away. Everything runs in your
        browser; the files are never uploaded. The hand-ordered version is the
        <a class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-deep" href="/merge-pdf/">Merge PDF page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="ticket mt-6 p-5 sm:p-7" id="bp-tool" data-mode="merge">
      <div id="bp-tray" class="tray p-6 text-center cursor-pointer" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Pick PDFs">
        <p class="font-display text-xl font-bold">Drop PDFs on the tray, or click to pick them</p>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-soft mt-2">PDF · as many as you like · they stay on this device</p>
        <input id="bp-file" type="file" accept="application/pdf,.pdf" multiple class="hidden" />
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-2 mt-4 flex-wrap">
        <button id="bp-folder-btn" class="chip" type="button">Pick a whole folder</button>
        <input id="bp-folder-file" type="file" webkitdirectory class="hidden" />
        <button id="bp-sort" class="chip" type="button">Sort the tray by file name</button>
      </div>

      <ul id="bp-list" class="mt-6"></ul>

      <div class="grid gap-6 mt-6 md:grid-cols-[1fr_320px]">
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">The order is the list</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft text-sm leading-relaxed mt-3 max-w-md">
            Files merge top to bottom. Scanners and export tools usually name files in the
            order they were made, so the name sort gets most folders right in one click; the
            Up and Down buttons fix the rest.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">File spec</h2>
          <dl id="bp-spec" class="mt-2">
            <div class="spec-row"><dt>files on the tray</dt><dd>0</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <button id="bp-run" class="btn-primary w-full mt-5" type="button" disabled>Merge the batch into one PDF</button>
          <p id="bp-status" class="font-mono text-sm mt-4 leading-relaxed" aria-live="polite">Pick two or more PDFs to begin.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="bp-result" class="hidden mt-8">
        <div class="tear pt-5 flex items-center gap-4 flex-wrap">
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">Result</h2>
          <span class="stamp" id="bp-stamp">Done on your device</span>
        </div>
        <div id="bp-rows" class="mt-4 grid gap-1"></div>
        <a id="bp-zip" class="btn-primary inline-block no-underline mt-4 hidden" href="#" download>Download all as one ZIP</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">How it works</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The page opens each PDF, copies its pages into a new file in list order, and saves.
          Pages are copied, not rebuilt, so nothing is recompressed and nothing is lost. It is
          the fastest job on this bench: the whole 25-file test pack took 71 milliseconds of
          engine time.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Honest limits</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The limit is your device's memory, not a rule of ours: a tray of very large files on a
          small phone can run out of room, and if that happens your originals are unchanged. A
          file this page cannot read as a PDF is marked on the list and left out of the merge,
          in plain words, before you run the job.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 mb-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4">
        {faq.map((f) => (
          <article class="ticket-soft p-5">
            <h3 class="font-bold">{f.q}</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mt-1">{f.a}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqJson}></script>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={howToJson}></script>
  <script>
    import '../scripts/batch-pdf.js';
  </script>
</Base>
